            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0854" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/87.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 440.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s telegram of
                    the 21st instant, in regard to the detail of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scorpion</hi> as stationnaire at Constantinople, I
                    inclose for your further information copy of a letter on the subject addressed
                    by the Secretary of State to the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <p>When you shall be in touch with Lieut Commander Logan, you will advise him as to
                    the formalities, salutes, etc., in passing the Dardanelles.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d712-a1.xml" xpointer="d712-a1"/>
            </div>
